EV Battery Research - repository licensing map

Original Python scripts and tests: MIT (licenses/MIT.txt).
Original explanatory research documents and original catalog commentary:
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0).
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Attribution: EV Battery Research contributors, research snapshot 2026-09-10.

Third-party material is NOT relicensed by the licenses above.
About:Energy parameter captures and adaptations, including extracted parameter
and OCP/reference-curve exports, remain CC-BY-SA-4.0 with attribution to
About:Energy Limited and the original cited studies.
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The EPA schedule capture/derived schedule carries the separate EPA scientific /
educational use policy notice. Blanket commercial reuse is not cleared here.
https://www.epa.gov/web-policies-and-procedures/epa-disclaimers

See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and metadata/license_map.json for file-level scope.
Source-page links and catalog entries do not grant permission to redistribute
uncollected external datasets. The repository has mixed licenses; it is not an
all-MIT dataset. Review the source conditions before publication or commercial use.
